    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n3011" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀκατά-σκευος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>lacking equipment</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πλοῖα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>PEdgar</u>
					8.4
				</span></i>
			
			<span class="entity">(iii B. C.)</span>; of savage tribes, <i><span class="en">
				Theagen.
				17
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> in Lit.
			Crit., <i>without artifice</i> or <i>elaboration</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Phld.
				<u>Rh.</u>
				1.8S.
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				D.H.
				<u>Th.</u>
				27
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Philostr.
			</span></i><i>V A</i><i><span class="en">
				6.11
			</span></i>; epith. of orator, <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				2.835b
			</span></i>. Adv.
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-ως</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Plb.
					6.4.7
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>III.</b>
			<i>uncivilized</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">βίος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					D.S.
					5.39
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>IV.</b>
			<i>disordered</i>, v. l. for <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀπαρασκ.</span>, <i><span class="en">
				Aeschin.
				3.163
			</span></i>.</div>
